invariant: INV-26
file: aes_block.h
catches: test/quic-builds.sh
reason: aes_block.h stops refusing a host object beside AES=extern, so a
  tree with its own build system compiles aes_hw.c and aes_extern.c into
  one object. Both define aes_block.h's entries, and the object's link
  then names a duplicate symbol, not the build choice that caused it.
  quic-builds.sh compiles aes_block.h under both defines and requires the
  refusal at the preprocessor.

--- old
#if defined(CH_CPU_RUNTIME) && defined(CH_AES_EXTERN)
#error "CH_AES_EXTERN is a device object's AES: a host object holds the AES instructions"
#endif
--- new
